exercises.task:
Java:
interface Flyable {
  void fly();
}
class Bird implements Flyable {
  public void fly() { System.out.println("soaring"); }
}
Flyable f = new Bird();
f.fly(); // soaring

JavaScript has no interfaces — any object with a fly() method works. Write a Bird class with fly() and call it, printing the same line.
